{{~!--
  Right-aligns an already-formatted figure in a fixed 14-character column, so
  that a stack of them lines its decimal points up in the monospace <pre> the
  notices are read in:

      Quantity         :   1,900,000.00 Bbls
      Quantity On Board:     950,000.00 Bbls
      Loading Rate     :      25,000.00 Bbls/Hr

  Called as {{> figure_col value=quantity}}. The figures reach the template
  already grouped to two decimals by formatCargoFigure ("1,900,000.00"), so
  only the leading padding is left to do.

  How it pads without a helper: EmailTemplateService compiles these templates
  in an isolated Handlebars environment that registers partials and nothing
  else — there is no padStart to call. But `lookup` on a string returns the
  character at an index, or undefined past the end, so
  {{#unless (lookup value N)}} is true exactly when the value is 14 - N
  characters or shorter. One space per out-of-range index therefore emits
  exactly (14 - length) spaces.

  A figure wider than the column is printed in full and simply pushes the line
  out — never truncated. Cargo quantities are what a bill of lading is drawn
  from; losing a digit to a column width is not a failure mode we accept.

  WIDTH = 14. Keep in sync with the frontend, which rebuilds this same block —
  see the note above the parcel block in 02_statement_of_facts/07_cargo_update.hbs.
--~}}
